<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_warrior_strengthofarms.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Protection Warrior Trinkets in Phase 3</span></h2>Your trinket usage will be dictated by what it is that you and your raid need. A stamina trinket like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96555/soul-barrier">
<img alt="Soul Barrier" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_warlock_demonsoul.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Barrier</span></a> will make you the least likely to die, especially in a 25-man raiding environment, while a trinket like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94508/brutal-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_strengthofarms.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> can offer a blend of defensive utility and offensive utility through the raw secondary stats and the Strength proc effect. Trinkets like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96543/gaze-of-the-twins">
<img alt="Gaze of the Twins" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_spectralsight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gaze of the Twins</span></a> have a more offensive tilt, but we scale well with both Strength and Crit, both defensively and offensively, making it a very attractive trinket. <br/>
<br/>Changing trinkets on an encounter-by-encounter basis is encouraged.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ins>Offensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96543/gaze-of-the-twins">
<img alt="Gaze of the Twins" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_spectralsight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gaze of the Twins</span></a> - This trinket is our strongest offensive option, especially as we start gathering more and more crit. This trinket will be heavily contested, so I recommend bonus rolling the Twin Consorts while in Arms or Fury loot spec (you cannot get this trinket while bonus rolling in Protection spec).</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96501/primordius-talisman-of-rage">
<img alt="Primordius' Talisman of Rage" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_rampage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Primordius' Talisman of Rage</span></a> - This trinket offers similar utility to the trinket above, but does it slightly worse. This is a strong Warrior trinket and requires you to be in Arms or Fury loot spec to loot it through a bonus roll.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94508/brutal-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_strengthofarms.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> - This trinket might as well be in both the offensive and defensive sections of this guide. It provides valuable stats while also having a proc that roughly lines up with our <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=1719/recklessness">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_criticalstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Recklessness</span></a> window. It's only slightly worse than the options above, but is extremely easy to acquire, requiring only Friendly with <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1435/shado-pan-assault">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> and 1,750 Valor Points.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=93256/skullrender-medallion">
<img alt="Skullrender Medallion" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skullrender Medallion</span></a> - This trinket requires Revered with <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1375/dominance-offensive">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dominance Offensive</span></a> but will be your best offensive option by far while providing decent defensive utility. It can also be upgraded twice, unlike a lot of the other options on this list.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77530/ghost-iron-dragonling">
<img alt="Ghost Iron Dragonling" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_head_dragon_bronze.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ghost Iron Dragonling</span></a> - Can be socketed with any stat of your choosing through Tinker's Gear sockets like <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77544/flashing-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Flashing Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flashing Tinker's Gear</span></a>. Shares Tinker's Gear slots with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a> if you're an Engineer.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> - Offers <b>a lot</b> of avoidance through the Strength to Parry conversion and is your best offensive trinket in fights where you don't get super high Vengeance. It's a very expensive trinket to purchase, and don't feel bad about missing out on it, especially if you're raiding in a 25 man environment.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81138/carbonic-carbuncle">
<img alt="Carbonic Carbuncle" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Carbonic Carbuncle</span></a> - This trinket brings less defensive utility than the other options on this list, but has a very strong 30 sec proc which translates into a lot of damage during your opener with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=1719/recklessness">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_criticalstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Recklessness</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=114207/skull-banner">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/warrior_skullbanner.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skull Banner</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=12292/bloodbath">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_bloodbath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodbath</span></a>. Has a long ICD, so may not be worth using on some fights.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Defensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96555/soul-barrier">
<img alt="Soul Barrier" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_warlock_demonsoul.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Barrier</span></a> - This is by far your best defensive trinket in Phase 3 and is realistically the only fully defensive trinket worth considering.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=91210/tyrannical-gladiators-emblem-of-tenacity">
<img alt="Tyrannical Gladiator's Emblem of Tenacity" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_endlessrage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tyrannical Gladiator's Emblem of Tenacity</span></a> - The second-best defensive trinket in Phase 3 comes from PVP. This trinket can also be used effectively in fights where you get Vengeance cap in order to extend that cap with the on-use health effect. The trinket's on-use does not share cooldown with other trinkets or tinkers.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96471/ji-kuns-rising-winds">
<img alt="Ji-Kun's Rising Winds" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_heal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ji-Kun's Rising Winds</span></a> - This trinket is a bit of an outlier and provides a somewhat balanced profile. It has A LOT more value in 10-man than in 25-man, and granted you can get your hands on this trinket to replace a Phase 2 trinket, I would recommend it.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79329/relic-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Relic of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_ox.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Niuzao</span></a> - This is a solid defensive trinket until you get another option from the raid. The 8871 Dodge also translates into solid offensive utility.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87160/stuff-of-nightmares">
<img alt="Stuff of Nightmares" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_trinketpanda_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Stuff of Nightmares</span></a> - This trinket offers less defensive utility than the Stamina counterparts, but does bring more offensive utility through reforging the Mastery and its Dodge proc effect. The value of the proc can vary greatly depending on the fight cadence.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87063/vial-of-dragons-blood">
<img alt="Vial of Dragon's Blood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vial of Dragon's Blood</span></a> - Similar to the above alternative, just worse.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="reputation">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
